      "successfulRequestCount": 1,
      "loggedRequestAttempts": 1,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 138,
      "outputTokens": 928,
      "costUsd": 0.008421,
      "pronunciationText": "Some rates go negative. Water moves through a gate into a dam at a rate of eight minus two t megalitres per day, for six days. After day four the rate is negative, so water flows back out through the gate. The integral from zero to six is twelve, and that's the net change: the dam ends up with twelve megalitres more than it started with. But the water that passed through the gate is the total area, sixteen in plus four out, which is twenty megalitres. So the question decides. If it asks how much the amount changed, use the integral. If it asks how much flowed in total, use the area."
    },
