      "costUsd": 0.006235999999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "The channel is thirty metres long, so it holds four thirds times thirty, which is forty cubic metres of water. A check with x gives the same answer. The two by one rectangle, minus the area under the curve, is two minus two thirds, which is four thirds. And here's a surprise. Double the depth to two metres, and the water's area nearly triples, because the channel is wider higher up."
    },
